    "q-22371": {
      "dom_id": "step-q22371",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find $n$ such that  ${a}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{3}\\cdot {a}^{4}={a}^{n}$  is correct.",
      "worked_solution": "We add the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}\\cdot {a}^{3}\\cdot {a}^{4} & = \\\\ {a}^{(2+3+4)} & = \\\\ {a}^{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore ${a}^{n}={a}^{9}$, so $n=9.$",
