      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Use exponents to rewrite the product $2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot 3\\cdot 3.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can apply the product rule to the two numbers independently:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot 3\\cdot 3 & = \\\\ ({2}^{1}\\cdot {2}^{1}\\cdot {2}^{1})({3}^{1}\\cdot {3}^{1}\\cdot {3}^{1}) & = \\\\ {2}^{3}\\cdot {3}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
